ep_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "Across the whole 30k window every active member of the group contacts the same fixed ~30-node core (57,156,234,...,1893). Members take turns being active (103 early, 866 mid, 1318/1374/1598/1826 late), so per-node activity looks like it starts and stops, but the contact identities before and after any candidate change point are essentially identical (Jaccard ~1). No old contact set is replaced by a new one; the only differences are sporadic one-off partners consistent with background turnover. High and uniform event volume (step_02) and the mid-window rate dip (step_03) do not correspond to any change in partner identity, so the regime-switch signature is absent."}, "raw_final_response": "**Analysis summary**\n\nThe group members all interact with an essentially identical core partner set: {57, 156, 234, 235, 255, 324, 354, 402, 535, 559, 617, 641, 728, 756, 874, 931, 1010, 1133, 1141, 1182, 1312, 1357, 1416, 1422, 1436, 1538, 1656, 1779, 1838, 1893}. What varies across time is *which group member* is emitting events, not *whom* they contact:\n\n- 103: this core set in [25166,30166], then almost nothing after (step_18, step_19, step_20, step_11)\n- 719, 462, 1224: same core set in [25166,40166], then only 1\u20135 idiosyncratic partners afterwards (steps 21/22, 14/15, 23/24)\n- 866: same core set in [35166,40166], then nothing (step_26, step_31)\n- 1318: same core set in [40166,45166] (step_32), empty just before (step_27)\n- 1374: empty early, then same core set in [40166,50166] (steps 04\u201308)\n- 1598, 1826: near-silent in [25166,40166], then the same core set in [40166,55166] (steps 12/13, 16/17)\n\nSo the \"before\" contact set and the \"after\" contact set around any candidate change point (e.g. t\u224840166, where the event-rate dip in step_03 occurs) are the *same* set \u2014 Jaccard \u2248 1 on the partner identities. There is no old-set \u2192 new-set replacement; the apparent temporal structure is a relay/staggering of activity among the group members over a fixed neighbourhood, plus a small amount of one-off background turnover (733, 511, 1536, 1370, 302/959/1114/1354/1683, 1106, 488, 1088). Total volume is high and uniform per node (step_02), which by itself could be mistaken for a signal \u2014 hence the controls.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_459f9d4b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [103, 462, 719, 836, 866, 1224, 1318, 1374, 1415, 1598, 1610, 1826],\n  \"window\": [25166, 55166],\n  \"confidence\": 0.78,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Across the whole 30k window every active member of the group contacts the same fixed ~30-node core (57,156,234,...,1893). Members take turns being active (103 early, 866 mid, 1318/1374/1598/1826 late), so per-node activity looks like it starts and stops, but the contact identities before and after any candidate change point are essentially identical (Jaccard ~1). No old contact set is replaced by a new one; the only differences are sporadic one-off partners consistent with background turnover. High and uniform event volume (step_02) and the mid-window rate dip (step_03) do not correspond to any change in partner identity, so the regime-switch signature is absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 42398, "total_output_tokens": 7882, "total_tokens": 50280, "total_latency_ms": 111788, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}